 # fastunknot 0.3.0: braid and structural certificates with optional shared backends
+
+## Quadratic periodic scheduling and weighted disk components (2026-10-09)
+
+The default interval merger scheduler is now `adaptive`. It preserves the
+historical complete reduction trace, using a bounded restart-scan prelude and
+then a generation-checked event queue when the scan allowance is exhausted.
+Use `merger_scheduler='legacy'` or `'queue'` for controlled comparisons.
+A closure with `k` rows uses at most `(k-1)**2` merger tests in queue mode;
+adaptive mode adds at most `k*(k-1)//2` tests. The queue has quadratic worst-case
+memory. Easy first-pair successes use a lazy fast path without queue setup.
+These are per-closure bounds, not a quadratic bound for all AHT cycles.
+
+`fastunknot.weighted_orbits.weighted_orbit_profile` computes compressed signed
+vector sums per orbit. `replay_weighted_orbit_profile` reuses an independently
+checked local trace. Equal vectors are grouped with binary multiplicities;
+neither interval points nor components are expanded. Full-carrier range
+transfer preserves a linear bound on active weight breakpoints. This is an
+implementation of classical weighted Agol–Hass–Thurston theory.
+
+`fastunknot.normal_component_profile.normal_component_profile` detects and
+counts compressing-disk components in a supplied admissible normal vector,
+including disconnected surfaces. Five integer weights recover component Euler
+characteristic, polygon count, boundary vertices, and two torus-cycle
+intersection counts. Set `record_certificate=True` and check the result with
+`verify_normal_component_profile(triangulation, coordinates, certificate)`.
+The old whole-surface `compressing_disk` flag is unchanged. A negative component
+answer concerns only that vector and does not prove boundary incompressibility.
+No correspondence with an input knot diagram is certified by this interface.
+
+Run `python -m component_profile_research.demo` for a meridian-plus-vertex-link
+example and a one-record certificate for `2**5000` parallel meridian disks.
+The demo requires no Regina. Independent Regina oracles are in
+`component_profile_research/oracles.py`. The accompanying research article,
+raw paired measurements, standalone snapshot, and integration patch are titled
+*Compressed Component Certificates and Quadratic Periodic Scheduling for
+Unknot Recognition* (9 October 2026). They establish local improvements, not a
+general quasi-polynomial unknot-recognition theorem.
+
 
 Orbit queries can now return independent local proofs with
 `count_orbits(..., record_certificate=True)`. Replay with
